<title>ITALY: Rolo in free 100 bln lire capital issue.</title>
<headline>Rolo in free 100 bln lire capital issue.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>One of Italy's largest banks Rolo Banca 1473 said it will propose a free capital issue of around 100 billion lire worth of shares at an extraordinary shareholders meeting on February 7 next year.</p>
<p>A bank statement said that it proposed to increase its share capital to 435.073 billion lire from 334.671 billion lire with the issue of 100.401 million new share of 1,000 lire each. These new shares would be distributed in the ratio of three new shares for every ten shares held.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
